# Keep the Docker/Fly build context small. Without this, the whole app/ tree
# (node_modules, uv .venvs with torch+eclipse-sumo, .next, the 41 MB SUMO net) is
# uploaded as context — ~3 GB, which is slow and can crash the builder. The API image
# only needs packages/kernel + apps/api SOURCE (see Dockerfile.api).

# Node / web (the API image never builds the frontend — Vercel does)
**/node_modules
apps/web

# Python virtualenvs + caches
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Build outputs
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info

# Large gitignored data assets — these live on the Fly /data volume, NOT the image
packages/kernel/data
packages/data/raw
**/.chroma*

# Local env + secrets (set via `fly secrets`, never baked into the image)
**/.env
**/.env.*

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.vscode
**/.idea
